        "type": "p",
        "text": "LIV removes tattoos with the Lucas pico laser. A picosecond pulse is about 1,000 times shorter than that of a conventional nanosecond laser, so the ink is shattered into finer particles with less heat build-up in the surrounding skin. The fragments are then absorbed by the body's immune cells (macrophages) and cleared through the lymphatic system — which is why removal takes a series of sessions rather than one visit."
